Reasoning: The greedy alone gets stuck in local optima (e.g., all models pile onto one GPU early). The move-based local search repeatedly relocates models off the worst-KVPR GPU whenever it strictly reduces the global max, which previously improved the score from ~23 to ~25 in the multi-start variants. Keeping only the move phase (no swaps) keeps the code short and fast while recovering most of the benefit.
